## Pitfalls

- **Missing flux biases outer rotation.** 2014ApJ...796..131O: resolved-out large scales overestimate rotation
  at large radii, so fit only R<100 AU. 2018ApJ...859..111H had no single-dish data to check resolved-out
  12CO. Filter models with simobserve (2015ApJ...812...27A) or add ACA/TP data.
- **Resolution bias in the break radius.** Mean-position fits underestimate R_b when resolution is limited
  (2015ApJ...812...27A); correct it, or test the method on model PV diagrams (2020ApJ...893...51S).
- **Inclination is weakly constrained and degenerate.** 2015ApJ...812...27A could not constrain i from its disk
  model; 2020ApJ...893...51S could not measure the outer disk inclination independently; 2021A&A...646A...1K
  reports a k-i degeneracy. M* scales as 1/sin^2 i, so propagate it. Even the sign matters: 2015ApJ...812...59O
  found +5 deg reproduced all PV cuts and -5 deg did not.
- **Self-absorption and optical depth.** 2017ApJ...843...27L weighted its fit to the blueshifted side because
  of redshifted self-absorption; 2014ApJ...791..123W treats the absorption dip as optically thick;
  2013A&A...560A.103M could not separate infall plus Keplerian from pure Keplerian in the outer 30 AU because
  of low S/N and foreground absorption.
- **Continuum subtraction can erase or fake absorption.** Fit inverse P-Cygni profiles on non-subtracted data
  (2018A&A...615A.141B); 2024AJ....167...94H shows continuum subtraction leaving a negative image of a clump.
- **Outflow contamination.** 2025SciA...11.4512O excluded the redshifted streamer from methanol analysis for this
  reason; 2014ApJ...796....1T notes missing flux and outflow complicate lines near systemic velocity.
- **Do not assume free fall.** Measured infall is ~0.3 V_ff in 2015ApJ...812...27A and 2017ApJ...849...56A, and
  2025SciA...11.4512O states infall there is neither free-fall nor viscous.
- **Non-unique models.** 2019A&A...623A..96Y: evolutionary time and relative velocity not unique;
  2018ApJ...859..111H: genetic-algorithm solution may not be unique; 2020A&A...634L..12D: no combination of
  Rd and theta0 reproduced the wide redshifted component.
- **Errors that are not propagated.** TIPSY does not propagate errors in fixed parameters (stellar mass,
  distance, Vsys) (2024A&A...683A.133G). By-eye fits give no formal uncertainties (2015ApJ...812...27A,
  2016ApJ...824...88O, 2019ApJ...873...73Z).
- **Masses and j are limits.** Optically thin streamer masses are lower limits (2024A&A...683A.133G); a
  continuum mass is an upper limit under the optically thin assumption (2025SciA...11.4512O); specific angular
  momentum can be only an upper limit (2016ApJ...832..158Z).
- **Unstated settings.** Pack aggregates: CASA version not stated in 20 cards, self-calibration solution
  intervals in 16, continuum subtraction and line-free channels in 16 (plus similar phrasings 14, 10, 9).
  Record these and the PV cut width.

## Verification checks

What the papers did:
- Compare single and double power-law fits by reduced chi2: 1.6 vs 4.0 (2017ApJ...849...56A), 1.6 vs 2.0
  (2015ApJ...812...27A); sum of squared residuals per dof (2014ApJ...796..131O).
- Leave Vsys free and confirm it (2017ApJ...849...56A recovered 5.8 km/s).
- Test the extraction method on synthetic Keplerian PV diagrams (2020ApJ...893...51S) and analyse resolution
  bias (2015ApJ...812...27A appendix).
- Try other geometries: spherical vs flattened envelope (2015ApJ...812...27A); density r^0 and r^-2.5 and a
  Keplerian-only model, which failed along the outflow direction (2016ApJ...824...88O); pure Keplerian with
  m* = 23 Msun rejected (2019ApJ...873...73Z).
- Vary the key model parameter: other infall radii (2015ApJ...814...22E); Rd and theta0 (2020A&A...634L..12D);
  a smaller 0.2 Msun mass (2014ApJ...796..131O).
- Check absorption is confined to the continuum with off-source spectra (2015ApJ...814...22E).
- Cross-check masses: SED-fit mass (2019ApJ...873...73Z), velocity-gradient dynamical mass
  (2024ApJ...967...15K), literature values (2017ApJ...834..178Y).
- Compare isotopologues: Keplerian radius from 12CO and 13CO/C18O ridge profiles (2025ApJ...993..120H).
- Validate trajectory code against N-body two-body runs with REBOUND (2024A&A...683A.133G).

What a careful referee adds:
- Show both major and minor axis PV diagrams with the model overlaid and residuals.
- Propagate inclination, distance and Vsys uncertainties into M*, r_CB, j and Mdot.
- Show that the result survives a change of emission threshold and of the excluded low-velocity range.
- Check optical depth with an isotopologue before reading line shapes as kinematics.
- State whether models were filtered through the same uv coverage, and quantify missing flux.

