### Limitations the authors admit
- 2017ApJ...849...56A: Resolution not high enough to resolve vertical structures; temperature profile fixed and vertically isothermal; abundance constraints weak
- 2015ApJ...812...27A: Inclination poorly constrained by the disk model; mass estimates are uncertain by optical depth, temperature, abundance
- 2015ApJ...812...27A: PV mean-position method underestimates break radius at limited resolution
- 2025A&A...693A..76C: Disk model is a toy proof of concept; H2CO method unreliable near the star
- 2020ApJ...893...51S: Outer disk inclination cannot be measured independently; non-axisymmetry not modeled
- 2018A&A...618A.120L: Launching-radius inferences rely on a steady-state assumption; ACA data would be needed to rule out an envelope
- 2016A&A...590A..73A: Resolution is insufficient for proper model fits; the jet mass is uncertain because of the CO-to-H2 conversion factor
- 2018A&A...614A.113H: Parameters tuned visually; no statement on fit quality
- 2018A&A...614A.113H: Insufficient spatial resolution limits kinematics
- 2018A&A...619A..39F: Candidate emitters unconfirmed; CO/[CII] profile differences need more data; Q is global average
- 2018ApJ...863..193V: The cavity is poorly defined and may not be real
- 2018ApJ...863..193V: HST images manually aligned, so small-scale offsets between gas and UV may be missed
- 2019PASJ...71..105T: Sidelobes of Sgr A* worsen sensitivity and remain in the continuum map; variability of Sgr A* limits data use
- 2021A&A...655A..25Z: Nuclear region barely resolved; higher resolution needed
- 2021A&A...655A..25Z: Cannot discriminate consecutive episodes from a decelerating wind
- 2018A&A...614A..42M: Only CO(2-1) available; cannot constrain temperature, pressure, heating
- 2020NatAs...4..670A: Uniform shell model over-simplified; results rough estimate
- 2020MNRAS.493.3744F: FIR SED poorly sampled so L_IR and SFR are lower limits; kinematics unresolved; SLED has too few points
- 2015A&A...580A...1M: Only one molecular line, so excitation mechanisms cannot be discriminated; X_CO uncertain
- 2015A&A...580A...1M: Jet orientation degenerate with lateral expansion velocity
- 2018ApJ...861...72C: Data did not initially pass QA2 due to low elevation and array configuration
- 2018ApJ...861...72C: Uniform sphere geometry is a clear limitation; masses are first-order
- 2015ApJ...811...92C: Model is parametric, not dynamically consistent, no systematic parameter search
- 2015ApJ...811...92C: MEM resolution varies with image
- 2025ApJ...993...90S: 12CO affected by foreground absorption; gas mass a lower limit
- 2025ApJ...993...90S: Dust mass depends heavily on opacity and temperature
- 2015A&A...584A..99E: Resolution insufficient to determine disc rotation axes and properties
- 2024A&A...685A..80Z: Clump C is tentative and needs confirmation; dynamical modelling is beyond scope
- 2015A&A...576L..15O: Flux lost to missing short spacings; large uncertainties in masses and orbital estimates
- 2020ApJ...889..140Y: Radial velocity of FS Tau A not calibrated; assumed from neighbours
- 2024A&A...689A.263D: Only qualitative arguments for the jet versus disk interaction
- 2024AJ....167...94H: Clump B Doppler velocity very uncertain
- 2024AJ....167...94H: Mass lower bounds for C and D; clumps poorly resolved
- 2024ApJ...963....1O: X_CO uncertainty may overestimate molecular mass by a factor of a few
- 2024ApJ...963....1O: Chandra data too shallow to resolve cavity
- 2018AJ....156..270S: Single thermal wavelength so beaming parameter cannot be determined; assumed parameters add about 5% to D and 10% to albedo uncertainty
- 2014ApJ...790..160S: Outflow quantities order-of-magnitude; XCO and line ratio uncertain
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Temperature poorly constrained by the data
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Calibration uncertainty not included in MCMC fit
- 2014ApJ...784...78R: Cannot tell whether gas lies in front of or behind the BCG
- 2018MNRAS.481.4931E: Velocity resolution is modest and dynamical modelling is deferred.
- 2013ApJ...776...77K: Inner radius only an upper limit; brightness exponent ill-determined; full radiative transfer model postponed
- 2017ApJ...834..178Y: Only three protostars with M*<0.1 Msun; larger low-mass sample required
- 2017ApJ...834..178Y: Masses and disk radii of IRAS 15398 and IRAS 16253 are lower and upper limits
