  - fitting: manual by-eye [4.1 The jet: "varying these until a good match with the map and PV diagrams was found by eye"]
  - validation: compared with SiO(2-1) results of Cesaroni et al. 1999 [4.1 The jet: "The only significant difference with respect to the values obtained by Cesaroni et al. ((cite: cesa99)) from lower resolution observations of the SiO(2–1) line"]
- step 4: Disk Trot and Ncol profiles from CH3CN
  - method: Extract TB along hyperbolic branches of DCN PV peaks; least-squares fit of eta*Trot*(1-exp(-tau)) over CH3CN K lines; power-law fits vs radius [Derivation of Trot and Ncol: "the best fit was obtained by minimizing the expression $\sum_i\left(T_{{\rm B}i}-T_{{\rm B}i}^{\rm mod}\right)^2$"]
  - software: GILDAS
  - parameter: lines K=2,3,4,5,7,8 and v8=1 K,l=2,1; at least three lines detected per pixel [Derivation of Trot and Ncol: "The calculation was done only for the pixels of the PV diagram where at least three lines were detected."]
  - assumption: LTE, density >1e7 cm-3 [Derivation of Trot and Ncol: "which can be analyzed under the LTE approximation given the large densities ($>10^7$ cm$^{-3}$"]
  - fitting: least squares, free eta, Trot, Ncol [4.2.2 Derivation of T_rot and N_col: "the best fit was obtained by minimizing the expression $\sum_i\left(T_{{\rm B}i}-T_{{\rm B}i}^{\rm mod}\right)^2$ , where the sum runs over the selected CH$_3$CN lines (see above). For this purpose, the free variables $\eta$, $T_{\rm rot}$, and $N_{\rm col}$"]
- step 5: Disk velocity field fit and envelope opacity
  - method: Minimize sum of squared LSR velocity residuals for CH3CN peaks with Keplerian+infall model; then vary tau0 to reproduce C-shaped peaks [Fit of the LSR velocity: "we minimize the expression $\sum_i\left(V_i^{\rm obs}-V_i^{\rm mod}\right)^2$"]
  - software: CASA
  - parameter: PA_d fixed to 48 deg; Rd=0.3"=490 au [Fit of the LSR velocity: "We fixed ${\rm PA_d}$ to the value obtained from a least-square fit to the peaks of all ground-state $K$ lines"]
  - assumption: kappa_d=0.01 cm2/g; halo density ∝ 1/r; dust-free optically thick thin disk [Fit of the C-shaped pattern: "where $\kappa_{\rm d}$ is the dust absorption coefficient that we assume to be equal to 0.01 cm$^2$g$^{-1}$"]
  - fitting: least squares [4.2.4 Fit of the LSR velocity: "To fit the disk velocity field, we minimize the expression $\sum_i\left(V_i^{\rm obs}-V_i^{\rm mod}\right)^2$"]
  - validation: model peaks qualitatively compared to observed C-shape [Fit of the C-shaped pattern: "We conclude that the model qualitatively mimics the C-shaped distribution of the data peaks"]
- result: Jet opening angle theta = 10 ± not stated deg [The jet: "$\phi$=3$^\circ$, $\theta$=10$^\circ$, and $V_0/R_0$=10 km s$^{-1}$ arcsec$^{-1}$"]
- result: Jet inclination to plane of sky phi = 3 ± not stated deg [The jet: "$\phi$=3$^\circ$, $\theta$=10$^\circ$"]
- result: Jet velocity gradient V0/R0 = 10 ± not stated km/s/arcsec [The jet: "$V_0/R_0$=10 km s$^{-1}$ arcsec$^{-1}$=1.3 km s$^{-1}$ pc$^{-1}$"]
- result: CH3CN Trot(R) = 1140 R(au)^-0.32 K ± not stated K [Derivation of Trot and Ncol: "T_{\rm rot}({\rm K}) = 107~\left[\theta({\rm arcsec})\right]^{-0.32} = 1140~\left[R({\rm au})\right]^{-0.32}"]
- result: CH3CN Ncol(R) = 1.7e19 R(au)^-1.3 ± not stated cm-2 [Derivation of Trot and Ncol: "N_{\rm col}({\rm cm^{-2}}) = 1.1\times10^{15}~\left[\theta({\rm arcsec})\right]^{-1.3} = 1.7\times10^{19}~\left[R({\rm au})\right]^{-1.3}"]
- result: Stellar mass, inclination psi, infall ratio A, Vsys = 12 Msun; 59 deg; 0.42; -4.3 km/s ± not stated mixed [Fit of the LSR velocity: "$V_{\rm sys}$=–4.3 km s$^{-1}$, $\psi$=59$^\circ$, $M_{\rm s}$=12 $M_\odot$, and $A$=0.42"]
- result: Envelope opacity tau0 and mass = 0.4; 6.7 Msun ± not stated dimensionless; Msun [Fit of the C-shaped pattern: "was achieved for $\tau_0=0.4$"]
