### 2020ApJ...893...51S: Disk Structure around the Class I Protostar L1489 IRS Revealed by ALMA: A Warped-disk System (2020; star_formation, protoplanetary_disks; observational_alma_primary)
- question: What are the structure and kinematics of the disk around the Class I protostar L1489 IRS at ~40 au resolution, and is the disk warped?
- step 3: Derive rotation profiles from PV diagrams
  - method: Gaussian fitting at each channel (inner, positions) or each position (outer, velocities within +/-2 channels of peak); power-law and double power-law chi2 fits [4.1 Velocity Structure: "We fit the following power-law function to the determined data points from the PV diagram by $\chi^2$ fitting"]
  - parameter: inner fit uses r<100 au [4.1 Velocity Structure: "we use only data points at $r<100 \au$ for fitting to the inner component"]
  - assumption: i=73 deg for stellar mass [4.1 Velocity Structure: "with $i=73 \ensuremath{^\circ}$, $V_{100}=3.20 \kmps$, and $r = 100 \au$"]
  - fitting: chi2 fit; errors from 10000 resamplings, 3 sigma [4.1 Velocity Structure: "as $3\sigma$ values of the posterior distribution"]
  - validation: Model PV diagrams of Keplerian disks used to evaluate bias of the fitting method [Evaluation of Fitting Method on PV Diag…: "we examine how correctly the new method derives the rotational profile."]
- step 4: Warped vs coplanar disk model comparison
  - method: RADMC-3D models of two disks added in image domain, observed with simobserve, compared to channel maps, moment maps and PV [4.2 Kinetic Model: "The produced disk models are observed using the CASA task *simobserve* with the ALMA antenna configurations similar to those in our observations."]
  - software: RADMC-3D, CASA
  - parameter: M*=1.6 Msun, Mdisk=0.0071 Msun, p=0.5, i=73 deg; inner 0.1-200 au PA 69; outer 300-600 au PA 54 [Table 2: "Disk outer radius ($R_\mathrm{out}$) | $600 \au$ |"]
  - assumption: h/r=0.03 (r/1au)^0.25, Keplerian, Semenov dust opacity, T*=4000 K [4.2 Kinetic Model: "The scale height is given by $h/r = 0.03\ (r/ 1\au)^{0.25}$."]
  - validation: Visual comparison [Kinetic Model: "The warped disk model matches the observations, while the coplanar disk model exhibits a clear offset from the observations in the P.A. direction."]
- result: Inner rotation power-law index p = 0.50 ± 0.11 dimensionless [Table 3: "$7.22\pm 0.09\ \kmps$ | $3.20\pm0.15\ \kmps$ | $0.50\pm 0.11$"]
- result: Central stellar mass = 1.64 ± 0.12 Msun [4.1 Velocity Structure: "The estimated central stellar mass after the correction is $1.64 \pm 0.12 \Msun$"]
