### 2017ApJ...834..178Y: Signs of Early-stage Disk Growth Revealed with ALMA (2017; star_formation, protoplanetary_disks; observational_alma_primary)
- question: When and how do Keplerian disks form and grow around Class 0 protostars, probed by gas kinematics at ~100 AU scales in three young protostars and a literature sample
- step 3: Fit outflow orientation and inclination
  - method: Compare 5σ 12CO moment 0 and P-V maps to wind-driven-shell model by minimizing residual sum, grid search over c0, PA, i, v0 [Appendix 7: "we arbitrarily assigned a value one to pixels above 5$\sigma$ in the $^{12}$CO moment 0 maps."]
  - parameter: PA in steps of 5 deg, i in steps of 5 deg [Appendix 7: "searched for the best $c_0$ and $PA$ in steps of 5$\ensuremath{^\circ}$"]
  - fitting: Residual-minimization grid search; errors from models with <15% larger residuals [Appendix 7: "we list the parameter ranges where our outflow models have $<$15% larger residuals compared to the best fits"]
  - validation: Compared with continuum aspect-ratio inclinations (~50 deg) and previous studies [4.1: "Our estimated inclination angle is consistent with theirs"]
- step 4: Measure C18O rotational profile
  - method: P-V diagram peak positions per channel fit with power law |V-Vsys|=Vrot(R0)(R/R0)^f with Vsys free [Appendix 8: "We included $V_{\rm sys}$ as a free parameter."]
  - parameter: R0 = 1''; low-velocity channels excluded [Appendix 8: "$R_0$ is an arbitrary characteristic radius and is set to be 1$\ensuremath{''}$"]
  - fitting: Monte Carlo, 1000 repeats varying data within uncertainties [Appendix 8: "We repeated this fitting process for a 1000 times, which is sufficient to reach convergence"]
- step 5: Fit kinematic envelope+disk models to C18O P-V
  - method: Infall+rotation+Keplerian disk model, LTE C18O images convolved with beam, chi2 fit to P-V; free n0, T0, M*, j; p in {-1.5,-2,-2.5} [Appendix 9: "Therefore, there are four free parameters in our kinematic model, $n_0$, $T_0$, $M_*$, and $j$."]
  - parameter: q fixed -0.4; envelope within 80 deg of polar axis zero density [Appendix 9: "$q$ was fixed to be $-0.4$"]
  - assumption: Free-fall infall, constant angular momentum, LTE [Appendix 9: "we computed the model images in C$^{18}$O on the assumption of local thermal equilibrium"]
  - fitting: chi2 minimization; uncertainties from varying one parameter to reduced chi2 min +1 [Appendix 9: "we varied one parameter at a time and kept others fixed at the best-fit values to search for the models having a reduced $\chi^2$ of the minimum $+1$"]
  - validation: Compared with analytical P-V results, Oya et al. 2014 and Hsieh et al. 2016 [4.3: "The precessing jet model for the CO emission in IRAS 16253$-$2429 (Hsieh et al. 2016) suggests the same central protostellar mass of 0.03 $M_\ensuremath{\odot}$ as our results."]
- result: Lupus 3 MMS rotational power-law index = -0.57 ± 0.03 dimensionless [4.2.1: "$V_{\rm rot} = (0.87\pm0.04) \times (R/R_0)^{-0.57\pm0.03}$ with $V_{\rm sys} = 4.62\pm0.04$ km s$^{-1}$"]
- result: IRAS 15398 rotational power-law index = -1.0 ± 0.06 dimensionless [4.2.2: "$V_{\rm rot} = (0.17\pm0.02) \times (R_{\rm rot}/R_0)^{-1.0\pm0.06}$"]
- result: Lupus 3 MMS protostellar mass (model) = 0.3 ± +0.09/-0.05 Msun [Table 2: "| Lupus 3 MMS | 150$^\circ$ | 60$^\circ$ | 0.3$^{+0.09}_{-0.05}$ | 130$\pm$70"]
- result: Lupus 3 MMS disk radius = 130 ± 70 AU [Table 2: "| Lupus 3 MMS | 150$^\circ$ | 60$^\circ$ | 0.3$^{+0.09}_{-0.05}$ | 130$\pm$70"]
- result: IRAS 16253 protostellar mass = 0.03 ± 0.01 Msun [Table 2: "| IRAS 16253$-$2429 | 112$^\circ$ | 60$^\circ$ | 0.03$\pm$0.01 | 6$\pm$6"]
- limitation (authors): Only three protostars with M*<0.1 Msun; larger low-mass sample required [5.3: "However, the number of the protostars with $M_* < 0.1$ $M_\odot$ in our sample is only three."]
- limitation (authors): Masses and disk radii of IRAS 15398 and IRAS 16253 are lower and upper limits [4.3: "the protostellar masses of IRAS 15398$-$3559 and IRAS 16253$-$2429 derived from our kinematic models can be considered lower limits"]
- not stated (card): CASA version and pipeline version; Line-free channels and continuum subtraction method for line cubes; Clean masks, threshold, image size and cell size; Which spectral windows/channels were used for continuum imaging; Details of the P-V cut widths and peak-finding procedure; Literature compilation values entering the Rd-M* fits, error treatment details (Monte Carlo priors)

